        {
          "signature": "",
          "thinking": "",
          "type": "thinking"
        },
        {
          "text": "We can't pay INV-104 because **the invoice is marked as disputed**. Only open invoices can be paid, so I can't propose a payment for it, and the policy layer would refuse one anyway.\n\nThe other checks are fine:\n- **Invoice:** 2,100.00 USDC from Contoso Grid Services for an emergency call-out on 14 October. It's due 2026-10-30.\n- **Vendor:** Contoso Grid Services is active, not blocked, and has a registered payout address on file.\n- **Existing payments:** None have been proposed for INV-104, so a duplicate isn't the problem.\n- **Vendor message:** It only describes the work. It doesn't ask for anything unusual, like a new address or urgent payment.\n\n**To pay it:** Whoever handles disputes needs to settle this one. If they decide the 2,100.00 USDC is owed and the invoice goes back to open, I can propose the payment to Contoso's registered address. You or another approver would still need to approve it before any money moves. I can't see why it was disputed, so whoever flagged it is the one to ask.",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ],
      "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
      "stop_details": null,
      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
